# Who has to approve a change before it lands.
#
# The `main` ruleset sets `require_code_owner_review`, which does nothing at all without
# this file: with no paths owned, no review is ever demanded and any single approval
# satisfies the gate. One line, one owner, so every path in the repository resolves here.
#
# Note that GitHub will not let an author approve their own pull request, so this cannot
# be satisfied on a pull request opened by the owner named below — those merge through the
# ruleset's bypass list instead.

